<title>PORTUGAL: Public buy offer for Totta shares denied.</title>
<headline>Public buy offer for Totta shares denied.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Businessman Antonio Champalimaud denied on Friday press reports that he was planning to launch a public offer to buy (OPA) for the outstanding shares of Banco Totta &amp; Acores, which his group controls.</p>
<p>&quot;I have not, nor have had, any intention to launch an OPA for the shares of BTA,&quot; he said in a statement sent to Portugal's Financial Markets Committee and a copy of which was obtained by Reuters.</p>
</text>
